From ef0235b9d64259e0801e98dc4ee4bf3c514cdba0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:01:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] l2r-local: bug 13b (runtime): cheaper pending stack, same
 order

The drop glue calls the pending stack's entry points for every cell it
frees, and with 0014 deriv and monadic-interp took 17% and 20% more user
cycles than the same programs built without 0014's codegen. Much of it
was bookkeeping: PENDING, DRAINING and RELEASES were three thread-locals,
the two Vecs with destructors (every access checked the destructor's
registration), every access went through a RefCell borrow flag, every
drain (even with nothing pending, as after most frees) ran the whole
function with its prologue, and every deferral and pop loaded the stack's
length and buffer before the top entry.

Now:
- One thread-local with no destructor: the stack by raw parts in Cells and
  the release table inline, so an access is only its address. The buffer,
  kept between drops, is freed at thread exit by a guard registered with
  the first buffer.
- The top entry, when it is a run, lives in the state itself and the
  entries below it in the vector: a deferral that links, and a pop, touch
  only the state's first cache line; freeing a cell whose members defer
  one cell never touches the vector.
- __reussir_drop_drain returns after a load or two with nothing pending or
  inside a drain, and releases a single pending cell without the general
  loop. The slow paths are nounwind extern "C" functions reached by tail
  calls, so the entry points need no saved registers.
- The table is emptied by a store, not a Vec::clear.

The entries, their order (last pushed first, a record's last member
first, host steps interleaved as before), the links through cell headers,
depth() and the public functions are unchanged. New tests (drop/tests.rs)
run random drops (deferrals wide and not, immediates, inline releases,
steps that push work, nested drains, more release functions than the table
holds) against a model with one entry per pending cell or step, and hash
every event with the depth() and active() seen then: the hashes are
identical with the previous implementation. They pass under Miri (strict
provenance, stacked and tree borrows).

User cycles (perf stat, min of 4 interleaved runs) over the same lean2rr
without 0014's codegen: deriv +17.5% -> +8.7%, monadic-interp +20.2% ->
+2.2%, cfold +5.3% -> +1.3%; binarytrees and rbtree unchanged.
